From 234dcef862683c24b74b3c34e804856bd65cd345 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaci32u4 <lucaci32u4@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 07:22:32 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve 'next' through account_login and honour it in the
 React login flow

Anything built on LoginRequiredMixin (django-oauth-toolkit's authorize view,
for example) sends anonymous browsers to /accounts/login/?next=... .
InvenTree redirects that route to the frontend and drops the query string,
and the React login only honours router state, so such a flow cannot resume
after the user signs in.

Backend: AccountLoginRedirectView forwards a same-origin 'next' to the
frontend (url_has_allowed_host_and_scheme) and drops every other parameter,
in particular the legacy ?login=&password= arguments, which must not end up
in the frontend URL.

Frontend: sanitizeNextPath() accepts same-origin paths only; getNextPath()
reads 'next' from the current URL or the router state; followRedirect()
prefers a valid 'next' (paths under the web base go through the router,
anything else through window.location.assign); keepNextState() carries
'next' between /logged-in, /login and /provider-signup; ProviderLogin()
makes the SSO callback_url /web/logged-in?next=... for the login process.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
